{"name":"Ilipur","status":"ok","title":"Ilipur","pageId":105059,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Ilipur\" title=\"Category:Maps of Ilipur\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Ilipur</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tVD.M_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tVD.M-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"aliases\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Aliases</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">\"Eyes and ears of <a href=\"/wiki/Elversult\" title=\"Elversult\">Elversult</a>\",<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs2-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Haunted Ilipur<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRPG4-p92_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRPG4-p92-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Town</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_Coast\" title=\"Dragon Coast\">Dragon Coast</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Interior_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Interior Faerûn\">interior Faerûn</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoD-p34_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoD-p34-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Large</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">2,432 in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs3-p143_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs3-p143-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Ilipur\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Ilipur\">Organizations in  Ilipur</a></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Ilipur</b> was a large port town located on the south-western shore of <a href=\"/wiki/Dragonmere\" title=\"Dragonmere\">the Lake of the Dragons</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoD-p34_3-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoD-p34-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Along with <a href=\"/wiki/Pros\" title=\"Pros\">Pros</a>, the towns were called the \"eyes and ears of <a href=\"/wiki/Elversult\" title=\"Elversult\">Elversult</a>\".<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs2-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Government\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Government</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Appearances\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appearances</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ilipur had a shallow harborage with no real docks. Trade ships' cargoes needed to be unloaded onto flat barges and dragged to shore. New ships were constructed on land and pushed into the sea as the town did not have dry docks.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs2-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Government\">Government</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Government\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Government\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ilipur was ruled by the Council of Burghers and a lord mayor. The lord mayor was in charge of the city's sheriffs, tax collectors, inspectors, and accountants, and all suffered from nepotism.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs2-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Traders from Elversult fully expected to pay fees and bribes to Burghers. They had little choice if they wanted to keep the cargo from the hands of local thieves and bandits.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs3-p143_5-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs3-p143-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ilipur and Pros served as loading and unloading points for Elversult's trade.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs3-p143_5-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs3-p143-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1370_DR\" title=\"1370 DR\">1370 DR</a>, the port towns of Ilipur and its neighbor, Pros, were used by the <a href=\"/wiki/Cult_of_the_Dragon\" title=\"Cult of the Dragon\">Cult of the Dragon</a> for the smuggling of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Magical_item\" title=\"Magical item\">magical items</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Scroll\" title=\"Scroll\">scrolls</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Material_component\" title=\"Material component\">material components</a>, and other goods that the Cult required in the areas of the <a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_Coast\" title=\"Dragon Coast\">Dragon Coast</a>. This operation made Ilipur a stage for numerous plots by the Cult, and opposing them were the <a href=\"/wiki/Harpers\" title=\"Harpers\">Harpers</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Astorians\" title=\"Astorians\">Astorians</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Teziir\" title=\"Teziir\">Teziir</a>, and the <a href=\"/wiki/Night_Masks\" title=\"Night Masks\">Night Masks</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Westgate\" title=\"Westgate\">Westgate</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoD-p34_3-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoD-p34-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a>, thieves of the <a href=\"/wiki/Purple_Masks_Guild\" title=\"Purple Masks Guild\">Purple Masks Guild</a> and slaver-bandits of the <a href=\"/wiki/Men_of_the_Basilisk\" title=\"Men of the Basilisk\">Men of the Basilisk</a> were present in the town and preyed on trade cargo unprotected by the Council of Burghers.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs3-p143_5-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs3-p143-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Following the calamity known as the <a href=\"/wiki/Spellplague\" title=\"Spellplague\">Spellplague</a>, by <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479 DR</a>, the town was doomed because of the receding waters of the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_of_Fallen_Stars\" title=\"Sea of Fallen Stars\">Sea of Fallen Stars</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Dragonmere\" title=\"Dragonmere\">Dragonmere</a>. With the livelihood gone, the trading town dried up and blew away.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs4-p116_6-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs4-p116-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Ilipur came to be known as <b>Haunted Ilipur</b> during that time. The empty seaport was littered with overturned skeletons of decaying ships. The town was not fully abandoned, however. A band of pirates called the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQmx1ZV9EYXduP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Blue Dawn (page does not exist)\">Blue Dawn</span> was in control of the remnants of Ilipur.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRPG4-p92_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRPG4-p92-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The town had a small handful of fair inns and taverns. There were no temples, but a few shrines to <a href=\"/wiki/Umberlee\" title=\"Umberlee\">Umberlee</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Lliira\" title=\"Lliira\">Lliira</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Tymora\" title=\"Tymora\">Tymora</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Tyr\" title=\"Tyr\">Tyr</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRcs2-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearances\">Appearances</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appearances\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Appearances\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><i><a href=\"/wiki/Azure_Bonds\" title=\"Azure Bonds\">Azure Bonds</a></i> (mention)</li>\n<li><i><a href=\"/wiki/Marco_Volo:_Journey\" title=\"Marco Volo: Journey\">Marco Volo: Journey</a></i></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ilipur?veaction=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRcs2-p80-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-2\">1.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-3\">1.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRcs2-p80_1-4\">1.4</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Julia_Martin\" title=\"Julia Martin\">Julia Martin</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Jeff_Grubb\" title=\"Jeff Grubb\">Jeff Grubb</a> (1993). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms_Campaign_Setting_2nd_edition_(revised)\" title=\"Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 2nd edition (revised)\">Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting 2nd edition (revised)</a>, A Grand Tour of the Realms</i>. (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc\" title=\"TSR, Inc\">TSR, Inc</a>), p. 80. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/1-5607-6617-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/1-5607-6617-4\">1-5607-6617-4</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRPG4-p92-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRPG4-p92_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRPG4-p92_2-1\">2.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Rob_Heinsoo\" title=